good evening this is my story this is my  song these are the words in blessed  assurance and I remember being on  Broadway watching Cicely Tyson on stage  sing those words and as I sat there i  started thinking about how amazing that  is so when I sort of think about what I  would say today I started to think about  those exact words this is my story this  is my song for those of you who don't  know  African Americans hold Sicily in such  high regard she is a queen to us we bow  to her  and it's not just because she was very  selective about the roles that she chose  over the years because she would only do  roles that served us as  african-americans it's not just because  she was an activist or a philanthropist  but it's because she was such a great  example an amazing woman with a good  heart and a good soul and we honor her  for just being who she is so when I  think about her life span you have to  understand this this is what's so  fascinating to me when she started this  business  it was Hattie McDaniels who had just won  the Oscar but she wasn't allowed to sit  down front she had to sit in the back of  the room first african-american to win  an Academy Award  she knew Josephine Baker she'd met  Josephine Baker she met Dorothy  Dandridge she was friends with Lena  Horne  she married Miles Davis I mean come on  so with all of that said I kept thinking  about that story this is my story this  is my song the day she called me and she  told me that she was going to get this  honor we sat on the phone for a while  and she was in tears I could hear it  because I can only imagine this woman  starting her career when black people  were not even allowed to come in to  front doors  wait I'm getting emotional thinking  about this because at that moment on the  phone was so powerful for me because  there she was having to do ten times as  much work and be paid a hundred times  less but she kept a smile about herself  she kept her wit she kept her way she  kept her class she kept her grades she  kept representing us and she remained  Cicely Tyson so for that  for that we thank you and I gotta say to  the Board of Governors my heart is so  full right now because I'm so grateful  and thankful to you for voting for this  woman because she so deserves it  she's so deserving it's been a long time  coming and as you go through the night  and you sing that song  blessed assurance praising my Savior all  the day long this is my story this is my  song here's another word you can add to  that song when you talk about your story  and that is oscar god bless you I love  you darling I love you so much
 

